hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"22876","Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us: Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Zaidah, from Asim ibn Kulayb, from his father, that a man of the Ansar informed him, who said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in a funeral. So when we returned, we were met by the caller of a woman of Quraysh, who said: O Messenger of Allah, indeed so-and-so invites you and those with you to food. So he turned, and we turned with him. So we sat in the sitting places of young boys before their fathers. Then food was brought, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, placed his hand, and the people placed their hands. So the people noticed him chewing a morsel, not swallowing it. So they lifted their hands and were unmindful of us, then they remembered, so they took our hands. So a man would strike the morsel with his hand until it fell, then they held our hands, looking at what the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would do. So he spat it out and threw it, and said: I find the meat of a sheep taken without the permission of its owners. So the woman stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, indeed it was in myself to gather you and those with you over food, so I sent to al-Baqi and did not find a sheep for sale, and Amir ibn Abi Waqqas had bought a sheep yesterday from al-Baqi, so I sent to him that a sheep be sought for me in al-Baqi and none was found, so it was mentioned to me that you bought a sheep, so send it to me. So my messenger did not find him, and found his family, so they handed it to my messenger. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Feed it to the captives."
